# Feature: runtime output. `io.print` renders its arg to a `str` and hands it to
# `sys.print`, which writes the {ptr,len} to fd 1 via libSystem `write`.
# expect: stdout "hello world\n"
# expect: exit 0
# String literals live in __cstring and are addressed PIE-safely with adrp/add; `write`
# is bound from libSystem via a chained-fixup into __got. (exit is still dyld's, on
# main's return.)
import std/io
fn main() {
    io.print("hello world\n")
}
